  "hints": [
    "Contrapositive: if x is even, then x³ − 1 is odd.",
    "With x = 2a, rewrite 8a³ − 1 as 2·(integer) + 1."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Contrapositive: if $x$ is even, then $x^3 - 1$ is odd.",
    "Suppose $x = 2a$. Then $x^3 - 1 = 8a^3 - 1 = 2(4a^3 - 1) + 1$, which is odd.",
    "So the original statement is true. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
